---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={"Test Systems | Roos Instruments"}
  description={"Cassini testers offer the industry’s broadest frequency and application range."}
  active={["nav-products"]}>
    <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - START
    =========================== -->
    <section class="breadcrumb-wrapper">
      <div class="container">
        <h2>Test Systems</h2>
        <ol class="breadcrumb">
          <li><a href="/index.html">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/products.html">Products</a></li>
          <li class="active">Test Systems</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>
    <!-- ==========================
    	BREADCRUMB - END
    =========================== -->


    <section id="content" class="container roosC">
      <div>
        <h2>Unlimited Test Capability</h2>
        <img id="UnlimitedTest" class="full-page" src="images/cassini_apps_range_140GHz.jpg"
          alt="Unlimited Test Capability - Spectrum of Applications" usemap="#image-map" style="top: -30px;">
        <map name="image-map">
          <area target="" alt="4G/LTE Communications" title="4G/LTE Communications"
            href="https://roos.com/parts/4G-CASSINI" coords="2,4,440,355" shape="rect">
          <area target="" alt="Power Amplifiers" title="Power Amplifiers" href="https://roos.com/parts/PA-CASSINI"
            coords="610,362,0,505,22,485" shape="rect">
          <area target="" alt="5G Communications" title="5G Communications" href="https://roos.com/5G"
            coords="893,359,444,0,819,67,1075,242,491,18" shape="rect">
          <area target="" alt="WiGig Communications" title="WiGig Communications"
            href="https://roos.com/parts/WIGIG-CASSINI" coords="891,361,614,503" shape="rect">
          <area target="" alt="Automotive Radar" title="Automotive Radar" href="automotive_radar.html"
            coords="901,0,1167,503" shape="rect">
        </map>
        <script is:inline>
          $(document).ready(function () {
            $('#UnlimitedTest').ImageMapResize({
              origImageWidth: "1200"
            });
          });
        </script>

        <div class="row">
          <div class="col-sm-10 col-sm-offset-1">
            <p class="main">
              Quite simply, our test platforms offer the industry’s broadest frequency and application range on the
              market. As the technology pushes for higher performance and wider frequency capabilities, be ready with
              Cassini.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <hr class="space">
      <div id="Cassini16" class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-6">
          <h2>CASSINI 16</h2>
          <img alt="Cassini 16" src="/images/Cassini16_view2_colorco_opt_web.png" class="centerImg leftImgAlignH1-H3"
            style="max-width: 462px">
        </div>
        <div style="position: relative; z-index: 1;" class="col-xs-12 col-sm-6">
          <hr class="space">
          <hr class="space">

          <style is:inline>
            .spec-line-1 {
              border: 1px solid #0849A1;
              opacity: 1;
              margin-bottom: 5px;
              margin-right: 15px;
            }

            .spec-line-2 {
              border: 1px solid #0849A1;
              opacity: 1;
              margin-bottom: 5px;
              margin-right: 15px;
            }

            tr:hover {
              background-color: #f5f5f5;
            }
          </style>

          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <div class="spec-line-1"></div>
              <span class="hidden-md hidden-sm">specifications</span>
              <span class="hidden-lg hidden-xs">specs</span>
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-9">
              <div class="spec-line-2"></div>
              <table style="width:100%; padding-bottom: 20px; border-spacing: 5px;">
                <tr>
                  <td>height</td>
                  <td>5.9ft | 1.8m</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>footprint</td>
                  <td>5.9ft | 1.8m</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>weight</td>
                  <td>220lbs | 99kg (equipped)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>electrical</td>
                  <td>100 to 220 VAC</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>consumption</td>
                  <td>&lt; 1 kW/hr</td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <div class="spec-line-1"></div>
              features
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-9">
              <div class="spec-line-2"></div>
              <p>16 instrument slot test head</p>
              <p>precision handler/prober docking</p>
              <p>applications from DC to 140 GHz</p>
              <p>instant multi-site scaling</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div> <!-- #Cassini16 -->
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-11 col-sm-offset-1">
          <p class="main">
            Cassini marks a new direction towards a completely modular architecture by making every part of the test
            system configurable. Bred from the same RF-centric foundation as its predecessor, Cassini supports drop-in
            measurement capability and scalable frequency coverage to provide targeted test resources and combine to
            build a complete production test solution.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="SPYDER" class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-5 col-sm-offset-1 col-sm-push-6">
          <h2 style="text-align: right;">CASSINI SPYDER</h2>
          <img alt="Cassini SPYDER" src="/images/SPYDER_2020_sm.jpg">
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-6 col-sm-pull-5">
          <hr class="space">
          <hr class="space">

          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <div class="spec-line-1"></div>
              <span class="hidden-md hidden-sm">specifications</span>
              <span class="hidden-lg hidden-xs">specs</span>
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-9">
              <div class="spec-line-2"></div>
              <table style="width:100%; padding-bottom: 20px; border-spacing: 5px;">
                <tr>
                  <td>height</td>
                  <td>2.4ft | 0.73m</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>footprint</td>
                  <td>1.9ft x 2.5ft | 0.58m x 0.76m</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>weight</td>
                  <td>95lbs | 43kg (equipped)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>electrical</td>
                  <td>100 to 220 VAC</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>consumption</td>
                  <td>&lt; 1 kW/hr</td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <div class="spec-line-1"></div>
              features
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-9">
              <div class="spec-line-2"></div>
              <p>8 or 16 instrument slots</p>
              <p>compact, cost-effective form factor</p>
              <p>turnkey solutions from DC to 140 GHz</p>
              <p>rapid development environment</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-11 col-sm-offset-1">
          <p class="main">
            Higher device complexity, shorter development times, and lower cost of test demand a breed of test
            equipment that’s more capable, more versatile, and more focused than ever. With Spyder, we’ve slimmed down
            traditional ATE while keeping all of the production muscle to deliver a completely integrated test solution
            in a compact size.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div> <!-- #SPYDER -->

      <hr class="space">
      <div id="CassiniARIA" class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-6">
          <h2>CASSINI ARIA V93k</h2>
          <img alt="Cassini ARIA" src="/images/Cassini_V93k_ARIA_web.png" class="centerImg leftImgAlignH1-H3"
            style="max-width: 462px">
        </div>
        <div style="position: relative; z-index: 1;" class="col-xs-12 col-sm-6">
          <hr class="space">
          <hr class="space">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <div class="spec-line-1"></div>
              <span class="hidden-md hidden-sm">specifications</span>
              <span class="hidden-lg hidden-xs">specs</span>
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-9">
              <div class="spec-line-2"></div>
              <table style="width:100%; padding-bottom: 20px; border-spacing: 5px;">
                <tr>
                  <td>height</td>
                  <td>0.7 m | 2.3 ft</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>footprint</td>
                  <td>0.8 sq m | 8.6 sq ft</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>weight</td>
                  <td>104kg | 230lbs (equipped)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>electrical</td>
                  <td>110 to 220 VAC</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>consumption</td>
                  <td>&lt; 1 kW/hr</td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <div class="spec-line-1"></div>
              features
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-9">
              <div class="spec-line-2"></div>
              <p>8 rf mmWaveinstrument slots (+4 DC & Digital from V93k)</p>
              <p>applications up to 140 GHz</p>
              <p>vector measurements and S-parameter characterization</p>
              <p>Advantest V930000 / SmartTest 8</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div> <!-- #Cassini V93k -->
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-11 col-sm-offset-1">
          <p class="main">
            CASSINI ARIA combines Roos Instruments' Cassini RF and mmWave technology with the Advantest V93000 platform
            to provide a unified test environment from DC to 140 GHz. By integrating vector measurements, S-parameter
            characterization, and advanced
            blind-mate interconnects directly into the SmarTest 8 workflow, ARIA enables efficient development and
            production testing of next-generation RF,
            mmWave, and mixed-signal devices.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="space">

      <style is:inline>
        .msc-spec {
          display: inline-grid;
          width: 110px;
          height: 110px;
          border: 2px solid #c0c0c0;
          z-index: 2;
          margin: 3px;
          vertical-align: middle;
        }

        .msc-spec p {
          margin: 0 auto;
        }

        .msc-spec span {
          font: Bold 1.5em Source Sans Pro;
          letter-spacing: 0;
          color: #00A7FF;
          text-align: center;
          margin: 0 auto;
          display: table-cell;
        }

        @media (min-width: 0px) and (max-width: 767px) {
          #Testhead {
            height: inherit;
          }

          #MSC-c1 {
            height: 380px;
          }

          #MSC-dots-1 {
            margin-left: 15px;
            position: relative;
            width: calc(100% - 15px);
            height: 200px;
            border-top: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-right: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-left: 0;
            border-bottom: 0;
            opacity: 1;
            z-index: 1;
          }

          #MSC-p1 {
            position: relative;
            z-index: 1;
            top: -198px;
            margin-left: 15px;
            width: 80%;
          }

          #MSC-p1 img {
            max-width: 200px;
          }

        }

        @media (min-width: 768px) {
          #Testhead {
            height: inherit;
          }

          #MSC-c1 {
            height: 520px;
          }

          #MSC-dots-1 {
            margin-left: 15px;
            position: relative;
            width: 455px;
            height: 200px;
            border-top: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-right: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-left: 0;
            border-bottom: 0;
            opacity: 1;
            z-index: 1;
          }

          #MSC-p1 {
            position: relative;
            z-index: 1;
            top: -198px;
            margin-left: 15px;
            width: 80%;
          }

          #MSC-p1 img {
            max-width: 200px;
          }

          #MSC-dots-2 {
            position: relative;
            top: -262px;
            left: 159px;
            width: 230px;
            height: 168px;
            border-top: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-left: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-right: 0;
            border-bottom: 0;
            opacity: 1;
            z-index: 1;
          }
        }

        @media (min-width: 992px) {
          #Testhead {
            height: inherti;
          }

          #MSC-dots-1 {
            margin-left: 15px;
            position: relative;
            width: 590px;
            height: 270px;
            border-top: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-right: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-left: 0;
            border-bottom: 0;
            opacity: 1;
            z-index: 1;
          }

          #MSC-p1 {
            position: relative;
            z-index: 1;
            top: -278px;
            margin-left: 15px;
            width: 80%;
          }

          #MSC-p1 img {
            max-width: 240px;
          }

          #MSC-dots-2 {
            position: relative;
            top: -246px;
            left: 210px;
            width: 297px;
            height: 202px;
            border-top: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-left: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-right: 0;
            border-bottom: 0;
            opacity: 1;
            z-index: 1;
          }
        }

        @media (min-width: 1200px) {
          #Testhead {
            height: inherit;
          }

          #MSC-dots-1 {
            margin: 0 0 0 15px;
            position: relative;
            width: 735px;
            height: 330px;
            border-top: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-right: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-left: 0;
            border-bottom: 0;
            opacity: 1;
            z-index: 1;
          }

          #MSC-p1 {
            position: relative;
            z-index: 1;
            top: -295px;
            margin-left: 15px;
            width: 80%;
          }

          #MSC-p1 img {
            max-width: 260px;
          }

          #MSC-dots-2 {
            margin: 0;
            position: relative;
            top: -193px;
            left: 247px;
            width: 350px;
            height: 260px;
            border-top: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-left: 2px dashed #4676B8;
            border-right: 0;
            border-bottom: 0;
            opacity: 1;
            z-index: 1;
          }

          .xl-no-left {
            margin-left: -30px;
          }
        }

        #Testhead h4 {
          position: relative;
          z-index: 1;
          margin-bottom: 1px;
          margin-left: 15px
        }

        .box {
          padding-right: 0;
          width: 135px;
          position: relative;
          min-height: 1px;
          padding-left: 15px;
          float: left;
        }

        .center {
          display: flex;
          justify-content: center;
          align-items: center;
          text-align: center;
          height: 200px;
          width: 125px;
          height: 125px;
          border: 0.5px solid #dddddd;
          padding: 10px;
          line-height: 25px;
        }

        .center p {
          font-size: 1.25em;
          margin-bottom: 0;
        }

        .strong {
          color: #00a7ff;
          font-weight: 900;
          font-size: 1.25em;
        }
      </style>

      <div id="Testhead" class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-6 col-sm-push-6">
          <img alt="Modular Testhead" src="/images/Cassini16_testheadview.png">
        </div>
        <div id="MSC-c1" class="col-sm-6 col-sm-pull-6">
          <h4>Modular, Configurable, Scalable</h4>
          <hr id="MSC-dots-1">
          <div id="MSC-p1">
            <p>Cassini’s backplane-less design allows for any instrument in any slot to optimize the test head for
              multisite, mixed signal topology, and feature expansion with up to:</p>
            <div class="row row-no-gutters">
              <div class="col-md-12" style="padding-left: 0;">
                <div class="box" title="QTY 15 x RI8535 Universal Digital TIMs">
                  <div class="center">
                    <p><span class="strong">1200</span><br>Digital Pins</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="box" style="padding-left: 11px;" title="QTY 16 x RI8546 Device Power TIMs">
                  <div class="center">
                    <p><span class="strong">544</span><br>DC Pins</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="box visible-xs" style="padding-left: 6px;"
                  title="QTY 13 x RI8545 TestSet 20 GHz + QTY 2x Sources + RI8587 Receiver 20 GHz">
                  <div class="center">
                    <p><span class="strong">52</span><br>Vector RF Ports</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row row-no-gutters hidden-xs">
              <div class="col-md-12" style="padding-left: 0;">
                <div class="box">
                  <div class="center" style="margin-top:5px">
                    <p><span class="strong">52</span><br>Vector RF Ports</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <hr id="MSC-dots-2">
        </div>
      </div> <!-- End #Testhead-->

      <div id="MSA" class="row xl-no-left">
        <div class="col-sm-4 hidden-xs">
          <img src="images/UltimateTestheadConfig2-Cropped.png">
        </div>
        <div class="col-sm-7 col-sm-push-1 xl-no-left">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col">
              <h3>Modular System Architecture</h3>
                <p class="main">
                  By fusing 30 years of test system integration with a configurable instrument architecture, Cassini
                  delivers a test solution that scales vertically to meet capacity needs while maintaining a cost
                  effective approach to capture emerging markets and disruptive technology.
                </p>
                <a href="products.html" title="Products">Learn More &raquo;</a>
            </div>

          </div>
          <hr class="space">
          <hr class="space">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <h5 style="text-align: center;">DC</h5>
              <img style="z-index: -1; max-width: 162px;" alt="DC TIM Interface" src="/images/blindmate_DCtim 2.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <h5 style="text-align: center;">Digital</h5>
              <img style="z-index: -1; max-width: 162px;" alt="DC TIM Interface"
                src="/images/blindmate_Digitaltim 2.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <h5 style="text-align: center;">RF</h5>
              <img style="z-index: -1; max-width: 162px;" alt="DC TIM Interface" src="/images/blindmate_rfTIM 2.png">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-3">
              <h5 style="text-align: center;">mmWave</h5>
              <img style="z-index: -1; max-width: 162px;" alt="DC TIM Interface" src="/images/blindmate_mmWave6.png">
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="row">
            <h5>Blind Mate Interface</h5>
            <p class="main">It’s the missing piece that transforms a set of modular instruments into a modular test
              system. The blind-mate interface creates a unified testhead from DC to millimeter wave without requiring
              specialized tooling or training. The setup provides a precise and consistent test interface while
              enabling better access to resources during development, quicker instrument servicing and calibration,
              and fast changeout in production.</p>
          </div>
          <hr class="space">
          <hr class="space">
          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <img style="z-index: -1; max-width: 350px; margin: 15px auto; padding:0;" alt="RIFL Communication Bus"
                src="/images/RIFLpath_Web.jpg">
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <h5>A Smarter Data Bus</h5>
              <p class="main">Roos Instruments Fast Link(RIFL) is the first open-standard data bus designed
                specifically for production test. Unwilling to compromise performance or functionality, we designed
                RIFL as a high-speed data bus and precision instrument power. It supports distributed compute packets
                across Cassini’s instruments to reduce data payloads and boosting system performance with real-time
                FPGA processing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div> <!-- End #MSA .row -->
      <hr class="space">
      <hr class="space">

    </section>
</Base>
